  {
    overview:
      "The Morytania area covers the entirety of Morytania along with the island of Mos Le'Harmless, Braindeath Island, Dragontooth Island and Harmony Island.<br><br>Instances of areas in Morytania and underground areas with an entrance in Morytania will also be included.<br><br>All transportation and teleportation via Charter Ships, Customs Officers, Gnome Gliders, Fairy Rings, Balloons and other forms of transport will require you to have unlocked access to the area your destination is in.<br><br>The following travel options are restricted unless you have access to the appropriate area:<br><br>- The Agility shortcut through the railing next to the Paterdomus Temple leading to Misthalin<br>- The stairs leading from the Paterdomus Temple up to Misthalin<br><br>",
    keyInfo:
      "Notable Settlements:<br><br>- Burgh de Rott<br>- Mos Le'Harmless<br>- Canifis<br>- Darkmeyer<br>- Meiyerditch<br>- Mort'ton<br>- Port Phasmatys<br>- Slepe<br>- Ver Sinhaza<br><br>Notable combat-related activities:<br><br>- Barrows<br>- Cave Horrors<br>- Fenkenstrain's Experiments<br>- Grotesque Guardians<br>- Haunted Mines<br>- Morytania Spider Cave<br>- Nightmare of Ashihama<br>- Lair of Tarn Razorlor<br>- Shades of Mort'ton<br>- Slayer Tower<br>- Theatre of Blood<br>- Vyrewatch Sentinels<br><br>Notable non-combat activities:<br><br>- Canifis Rooftop Agility Course<br>- Daeyalt Essence Mining<br>- Ectofuntus Prayer Training<br>- The True Blood Altar<br>- Hallowed Sepulchre<br>- Harmony Island Herb Patch<br>- Port Phasmatys Allotment Patch<br>- Temple Trekking<br>- Vyre Pickpocketing<br>- Werewolf Agility Course<br><br>The following Morytania shop stocks have been modified:<br>- Blood Talisman has been added to the Canifis General Store<br><br><br>",
    unlocks:
      'The following quests and their pre-reqs are automatically completed but will not reward any completion XP:<br>- Vampyre Slayer<br>- Taste of Hope<br>- The Great Brain Robbery<br>- Ghosts Ahoy<br><br>The following tasks in the Morytania Achievement Diary are automatically completed:<br><br>Medium Tasks:<br>- Make a batch of Cannonballs at the Port Phasmatys furnace<br>- Travel to Dragontooth isle<br><br>Hard Tasks:<br>- Enter the Kharyrll portal in your Player Owned House through a Portal Chamber<br>- Pray at the Altar of Nature in the Nature Grotto with Piety activated<br><br>Elite Tasks:<br>- Catch a shark in Burgh de Rott with your bare hands<br>- Fertilize the Morytania herb patch using Lunar spells<br><br>The following Combat Achievements are automatically completed:<br><br>- Theatre of Blood Veteran<br>- Theatre of Blood Master<br>- Theatre of Blood Grandmaster<br>- Theatre of Blood: HM Grandmaster<br>- Chally Time<br>- Nylocas, On the Rocks<br>- Faithless Crypt Run<br><br>',
    drops:
      'Theatre of Blood: Hard mode and Phosanis nightmare have the following changes:<br><br>- Damage & Defence increased by 25%<br>- 50% increased hitpoints on monsters<br>- Unique chance will be further multiplied by 2.<br><br>The drops listed below are affected by the drop rate modifier perks granted by passive Relic unlocks.<br><br>Drop rates affected are always rounded down and are not tied to area unlocks. This list represents the key drops affected in Morytania.<br><br>Group content like The Nightmare and Theatre of Blood will determine the drop rate modifier for their uniques from the MVP of that particular kill/completion.<br><br>- Black masks from Cave horrors.<br>- Barrows armour and weapon pieces from The Barrows<br>- Granite Gloves from Grotesque Guardians<br>- Granite Hammers from Grotesque Guardians<br>- Granite Rings from Grotesque Guardians<br>- Dark Tourmaline Cores from Grotesque Guardians<br>- Rings of Endurance (uncharged) from The Hallowed Sepulchre<br>- Blood Shards from Vyres.<br>- All unique rewards from the Theatre of Blood<br>- All unique rewards from The Nightmare<br>- All unique rewards from Superior Slayer Creatures<br>- Zealot Robes from Shades of Morton<br>- Runescrolls from Shades of Morton<br>- Granite Maul from Gargoyles<br>- Brittle Key from Gargoyles<br>- All unique rewards from Araxxor and Araxytes<br><br><br>',
  },
  {
    overview:
      "The Kharidian Desert area covers the entirety of the Kharidian Desert.<br><br>The Emir's Arena minigame will not be available during this League, although the building itself is accessible.<br><br>Instances of areas in the Kharidian Desert and underground areas with an entrance in the Kharidian Desert will also be included.<br><br><br>All transportation and teleportation via Charter Ships, Customs Officers, Gnome Gliders, Fairy Rings, Balloons or any other form of transport will require you to have unlocked access to the area your destination is in.<br><br><br>",
    keyInfo:
      "Notable Settlements:<br><br>- Bandit Camp<br>- Necropolis<br>- Ruins of Unkah<br>- Bedabin Camp<br>- Desert Mining Camp<br>- Nardah<br>- Pollnivneach<br>- Ruins of Uzer<br>- Uzer Oasis<br>- Giants' Plateau<br>- Sophanem<br><br>Notable combat-related activities:<br><br>- Bandits<br>- Kalphite Queen<br>- Pollnivneach Slayer Dungeon<br>- Tombs of Amascut<br>- The Leviathan<br><br>Notable non-combat activities:<br><br>- Agility Pyramid<br>- Mage Training Arena<br>- Giants Foundry<br>- Guardians of the Rift<br>- Nardah Elidinis Statuette<br>- Pollnivneach blackjacking<br>- Pollnivneach House Portal<br>- Pollnivneach Rooftop Agility Course<br>- Pyramid Plunder<br>- Fire Altar<br>- Sandstone and Granite Mining<br>- Sandstorm Machine<br>- Sorceress' Garden<br>- Zahur's Herblore Services<br>- Tempoross<br><br>",
    unlocks:
      "The following quests and their pre-reqs are automatically completed but will not reward any completion XP:<br><br>- Prince Ali Rescue<br>- The Golem<br>- Shadow of the Storm<br>- Icthlarin's Little Helper<br>- Temple of the Eye<br>- Desert Treasure II<br><br>The following tasks in the Desert Achievement Diary are automatically completed:<br><br>Medium Tasks:<br>- Travel to the Desert via the Eagle transport system<br><br>Hard Tasks:<br>- Slay a dust devil in the desert cave with a Slayer Helmet equipped<br>- Refill your Waterskins in the Desert using Lunar spells<br><br>Elite Tasks:<br>- Bake a wild pie at the Nardah clay oven<br>- Speak to the Kalphite Queen Head in your Player Owned House<br><br>The above Kalphite Queen Head diary task will complete when you receive a Kalphite Queen Head or Kalphite Queen Head(tattered) drop instead.<br><br>Near the Mage training arena entrance there will be a portal to Guardians of the rift.<br><br>The following Combat Achievements are automatically completed:<br><br>- Tomb Explorer<br>- Tomb Raider<br>- Tomb Looter<br>- Novice Tomb Explorer<br>- Novice Tomb Raider<br>- Novice Tomb Looter<br>- Expert Tomb Looter<br>- Expert Tomb Raider<br>- Insect Deflection<br><br>",
    drops:
      "Tombs of Amascut has 2 new invocations, meaning max raid level can go up to 1000<br><br>The drops listed below are affected by the drop rate modifier perks granted by passive Relic unlocks.<br><br>Drop rates affected are always rounded down and are not tied to area unlocks. This list represents the key drops affected in The Desert.<br><br>- The Pharaoh's Sceptre from Pyramid Plunder<br>- Dragon Chainbodies from all sources<br>- Dragon 2-handed Swords from all sources<br>- Dust Battlestaves from Dust Devils<br>- All unique rewards from Superior Slayer Creatures<br>- All unique rewards from Tombs of Amascut<br>- All unique rewards from The Leviathan<br>- All unique rewards from Tempoross<br>- All unique rewards from Guardians of the Rift<br>- Dragon pickaxe from all sources<br><br><br>",
  },
  {
    overview:
      'The Wilderness area covers the entirety of the Wilderness.<br><br>Last Man Standing and Bounty Hunter will not be accessible during this League.<br><br>For this League, deaths will behave differently in the Wilderness:<br><br>- PvP deaths will be treated like a PvM death with your lost items moving to a gravestone. The gravestone will then move to your respawn location.<br>- PvM deaths will be unaffected.<br>- Loot keys are disabled on League Worlds.<br><br>Instances of areas in the Wilderness and underground areas with an entrance in the Wilderness will also be included.<br><br>All transportation and teleportation via Charter Ships, Customs Officers, Gnome Gliders, Fairy Rings, Balloons and other forms of transport require you to have unlocked access to the area your destination is in.<br><br>The following travel options are restricted unless you have access to the appropriate area:<br><br>- Crossing the Wilderness Ditch will require access to whichever area is on the other side of it<br>- The lever at the Deserted Keep will work only if you have access to the area it takes you to<br><br>Demonic pacts will be disabled in PVP where possible.',
    keyInfo:
      "Notable Settlements:<br><br>- Bandit Camp<br>- Dark Warriors' Fortress<br>- Ferox Enclave<br>- The Mage Arena<br>- Rogues' Castle<br>- The Pirates' Hideout<br><br>Notable combat-related activities:<br><br>- Callisto and Artio<br>- Chaos Elemental<br>- Chaos Fanatic<br>- Corporeal Beast<br>- Crazy Archaeologist<br>- Forthinry Dungeon<br>- King Black Dragon<br>- Lava Dragons<br>- Mage Arena<br>- Mage Arena II<br>- Scorpia<br>- Venenatis and Spindel<br>- Vet'ion and Calvar'ion<br>- Wilderness God Wars Dungeon<br>- Wilderness Slayer Cave<br><br>Notable non-combat activities:<br><br>- Abyss Runecrafting<br>- Altar access is restricted to their areas<br>- Air Obelisk<br>- Black Chinchompas<br>- Black Salamanders<br>- Dark Crab Fishing<br>- Earth Obelisk<br>- Fountain of Rune<br>- Chaos Altar<br>- Wilderness Agility Course<br>- Wilderness Resource Area<br>- Rogue Chests<br><br>Access to the Revenant Caves will be free instead of requiring 100,000 coins to enter.<br><br>Access to the Wilderness Agility Course will be free instead of requiring 150,000 coins to enter.<br><br>Dying will not reset your lap counter in the Wilderness Agility Course.<br><br><br><br>Krystillia assigns tasks like any other Slayer Master, not assigning Wilderness-specific tasks.<br><br>Slayer targets defeated within the Wilderness will have a chance to drop a Larran's Key.<br><br><br><br>",
    unlocks:
      'The following quest is automatically completed but will not award any completion XP:<br><br>- Enter the Abyss<br><br>The Wilderness diary master has been relocated to Ferox Enclave and the following tasks in the Wilderness Achievement Diary are automatically completed:<br><br>Easy Tasks:<br>- Enter the Wilderness from the Ardougne or Edgeville lever<br>- Kill an earth warrior<br><br>Medium Tasks:<br>- Smith a Gold Helmet in the resource area<br>- Talk to the Emblem Trader<br>- Charge an Earth orb<br><br>Hard Tasks:<br>- Take the Agility shortcut from Trollheim to the Wilderness<br>- Fish a raw lava eel in the Wilderness<br>- Charge an air orb<br><br>Elite Tasks:<br>- Teleport to Ghorrock<br><br><br>The following Combat Achievements are automatically completed:<br><br>- Finding the Weak Spot<br><br>',
    drops:
      "The drops listed below are affected by the drop rate modifier perks granted by passive Relic unlocks.<br><br>Drop rates affected are always rounded down and are not tied to area unlocks. This list represents the key drops affected in the Wilderness.<br><br>- All unique rewards from Revenants<br>- Malediction and Odium shards from all sources<br>- Fedoras from the Crazy Archaeologist<br>- Dragon Boots from spiritual mages<br>- Dragon 2-handed Swords from all sources<br>- Dragon Pickaxes from all sources<br>- All unique rewards from Venenatis<br>- All unique rewards from Callisto<br>- All unique rewards from Vet'ion<br>- Draconic Visages from all sources<br>- Amulets of Eternal Glory from the Fountain of Rune<br>- Dagon'hai robes from Larran's Big Chest<br>- All unique rewards from the Corporeal Beast<br>- All unique rewards from Superior Slayer Creatures<br>- All unique rewards from Zombie Pirates and Zombie Pirate Lockers<br>- All unique rewards from Elder Chaos Druids<br>- Smouldering Stone from Hellhounds<br><br><br>",
  },
  {
    overview:
      'The Kebos and Kourend area covers the entirety of Kebos and Kourend.<br><br>Instances of areas in Kebos and Kourend and underground areas with an entrance in Kebos and Kourend will also be included.<br><br>All transportation and teleportation via Charter Ships, Customs Officers, Gnome Gliders, Fairy Rings, Balloons and all other forms of transport will require you to have unlocked access to the area your destination is in.<br><br><br><br>',
    keyInfo:
      "Notable Settlements:<br><br>- Hosidius<br>- Arceuus<br>- Lovakengj<br>- Port Piscarilius<br>- Shayzien<br>- Kingstown<br>- Northern Tundras<br>- Kourend Woodland<br>- Mount Karuulm<br>- Kebos Swamp<br>- Mount Quidamortem<br><br>Notable combat-related activities:<br><br>- Chambers of Xeric<br>- Lizardman Shaman<br>- Mount Karuulm Slayer Dungeon<br>- Sarachnis (Forthos Dungeon)<br>- Catacombs of Kourend<br>- Giants' Den<br>- Yama<br><br>Notable non-combat activities:<br><br>- Farming Guild<br>- Woodcutting Guild<br>- Arceuus Library<br>- Hosidius House Portal<br>- Tithe Farm<br>- Lake Molch Aerial Fishing<br>- The Wintertodt<br>- Soul and Blood Altar<br>- Blast Mine<br>- Hosidius Patches<br><br>Konar will assign Slayer Tasks based on the areas you have unlocked.<br><br><br>",
    unlocks:
      'The following quests and their pre-reqs are automatically completed but will not reward any completion XP:<br>- A Kingdom Divided<br><br>The following tasks in the Kourend and Kebos Achievement Diary are automatically completed:<br><br>Hard Tasks:<br>- Cast Monster Examine on a mountain troll south of Mount Quidamortem.<br><br>The following Combat Achievements are automatically completed:<br><br>- Chambers of Xeric Veteran<br>- Chambers of Xeric Master<br>- Chambers of Xeric Grandmaster<br>- Chambers of Xeric: CM Master<br>- Chambers of Xeric: CM GrandMaster<br>- Demonbane Weaponry<br>- No Pressure<br><br>',
    drops:
      "Chambers of Xeric: Challenge mode has the following changes<br><br>- Damage & Defence increased by 25%<br>- 50% increased hitpoints on monsters<br>- Unique chance will be further multiplied by 3.<br>- Dexterous and Arcane Prayer Scrolls have a weighting of 5 to drop instead of 20.<br><br>-The drops listed below are affected by the drop rate modifier perks granted by passive Relic unlocks.<br><br>Drop rates affected are always rounded down and are not tied to area unlocks. This list represents the key drops affected in Kebos and Kourend.<br><br>- All unique rewards from Chambers of Xeric<br>- All unique rewards from Wintertodt<br>- Dragon Thrownaxe and Dragon Knife from Drakes, Hydras and Wyrms<br>- Hydra's Claw, Hydra's Leather, Hydra's Eye, Hydra's Heart, Hydra's Fang and Hydra Tail from Hydras<br>- Drake's Tooth and Drake's Claw from Drakes<br>- Dragon Sword and Dragon Harpoon from Wyrms<br>- Dragon Warhammer from lizardman shamans<br>- Draconic Visage from dragons in the Catacombs of Kourend<br>- Sarachnis Cudgel from Sarachnis<br>- Bottomless Compost Bucket from Hespori<br>- Dusk Mystic and Dragon Hasta from the Brimstone Chest<br>- All unique rewards from Superior Slayer Creatures<br>- Hespori seeds<br>- Golden Tench from Aerial Fishing<br>- Soulflame Horn & Oathplate armour drops from Yama and his Forgotten lockboxes.<br><br>",
